{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"body":"Fix pushed for review as Gerrit change 2984, commit `592ac2afb3d`, branched from current `origin/main`.\n\nHow the HCL was brought across: the 3 spend-cap paths were checked out directly from `origin/bedrock-daily-spend-cap` onto a fresh `origin/main` worktree, rather than cherry-picking that branch's 2-commit history. That avoids importing the branch commit whose subject carried a literal threshold figure.\n\nCurrency scrub, since this lands in a public repository. Figures were removed from the branch commit subject, from `bedrock_spend_cap.tf` comments, and from `README.md` and `handler.py` doc comments - thresholds, worked examples, per-request costs, fallback rates, and a test threshold. Verified independently of the implementing agent's own scan: `git show HEAD --format= -U0 | grep '^+' | grep -inE '\\$[0-9]|[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)? ?(usd|dollars)|usd ?[0-9]'` returns nothing on the added lines, and the same pattern against the full commit message returns nothing. Remaining `USD`/`dollar` hits are currency terminology, config key names, HCL config units, and values formatted at runtime - no committed prose amount.\n\nTwo drift-plan items were deliberately NOT absorbed into this change:\n\n- `aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm.reviewbot_webhook_auth_rejections` (the 1 add) is kept. It belongs to closed ops bug `enrapt-capitalist-jackrabbit` and is an intended review-bot health alarm. The plan wants it added because it exists in HCL and has never been applied; the resolution is an operator apply, not deleting the HCL.\n- `aws_instance.gerrit` (the 1 change) is not reconciled. The plan shows an in-place `user_data` hash update only, and applying it restarts production Gerrit - outside the scope of a no-apply code restoration.\n\nValidation: `terraform fmt -check` passed, `terraform validate` passed, `rebar verify-commit-ticket --rev HEAD` passed. `make verify` exited 2 with 33 failures, all attributable to the documented current-main baseline - 17 pandoc/wiki-render, 10 doctor/lock, 6 sandbox/SemLock/local-IPC. No Terraform or spend-cap failure appeared.\n\nAC1 is satisfied in code and awaits landing. AC2 passes. AC4, AC5 and AC7 are recorded here. AC3 (clean drift plan) and AC6 (green `terraform-drift.yml`) can only be confirmed after this lands and the workflow runs, and AC3 will additionally require the operator apply noted above.\n\nExpect `Verified -1` on the first CI run for a reason unrelated to this change: `ddb1d953812` put an environment-dependent test on `main` that fails on any CI runner, currently red-lighting every patchset. Tracked on `rebuffable-pebbly-xenurine`. This change needs a recheck once that fix lands, not a rebase."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789722270445990001,"uuid":"4ef6824d-5c92-434e-922b-a5f3527153d0"}